					<description><![CDATA[<p>Ordway Secures $20M To Accelerate AI Finance Platform Ordway has secured $20 million in new equity and debt funding to expand its AI-powered monetisation and billing platform. The round was</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/ordway-secures-20m-funding/" data-wpel-link="internal">Ordway Secures $20M To Expand AI Billing And Revenue Platform</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<h2><b>Ordway Secures $20M To Accelerate AI Finance Platform</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Ordway has secured $20 million in new equity and debt funding to expand its AI-powered monetisation and billing platform. The round was led by Harbert Growth Partners, while Western Alliance Bank&#8217;s Innovation Banking Group provided the debt financing.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Ordway will use the funding supporting artificial intelligence initiatives, reporting enhancements, and overall business growth globally. Founded in Washington, DC, Ordway develops billing and revenue management software for technology-focused subscription businesses worldwide.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Its platform automates quote-to-cash workflows, simplifying subscriptions, billing, payments, revenue recognition, and financial reporting processes together. Ordway helps finance teams manage every revenue operation through one centralised platform improving efficiency and operational accuracy.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The funding reflects growing investor confidence in AI-powered financial operations software as businesses adopt increasingly flexible </span><a href="https://dealhub.io/glossary/pricing-models/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener external noreferrer" data-wpel-link="external"><span style="font-weight: 400">pricing models</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400">. Companies offering subscription, usage-based, and hybrid services require platforms that can manage complex billing while maintaining financial accuracy and compliance. </span></p>
<h2><b>AI Investments Target Finance Automation</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Ordway plans to use the funds to double its research and development funding and broaden its AI roadmaps for finance professionals with new automation solutions including the release of AI-enhanced cash reconciliation that reconciles payments from any number of bank accounts with invoices.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The platform also features AI contract data extraction, allowing businesses to automatically capture billing and revenue recognition information from subscription agreements. The company has also introduced MCP integration for Claude, extending AI-assisted capabilities across its platform.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Future development will focus on AI agents that automate routine financial tasks. These include updating billing records, accounting workflows, investor metrics, and contract modifications such as renewals or subscription pauses.</span></p>
<h2><b>Platform Expands Beyond Billing Into Payments</b></h2>
<div id="attachment_204060" style="width: 1322px" class="wp-caption alignnone"><img decoding="async" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-204060" class="size-full wp-image-204060" src="https://ventureburn.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Ordway-2.png" alt="Illustration of an AI-powered revenue management platform integrating payment processing, invoice reconciliation, and enterprise financial systems into a unified digital infrastructure." width="1312" height="736" /><p id="caption-attachment-204060" class="wp-caption-text">AI-powered revenue management platforms are transforming enterprise finance by unifying payment processing, invoice reconciliation, and automated financial operations within a single intelligent system. Source: Created by Ventureburn.</p></div>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Alongside its AI investments, Ordway is expanding into payment processing through the launch of Ordway Payments. The new offering is designed to simplify payment collection, invoice matching, and revenue reconciliation.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">According to the company, businesses increasingly require integrated finance systems as pricing models become more complex. Enterprise customers often operate across multiple legal entities, accounting systems, and reporting jurisdictions, increasing demand for automated financial infrastructure.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Chief Executive Officer Sameer Gulati said finance teams continue to face operational challenges after sales teams complete new customer agreements. Ordway said automation from point-of-sale systems into financial platforms remains a major industry trend driving adoption.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The company believes customers increasingly prefer unified revenue management instead of multiple disconnected financial software solutions. Ordway said its growth reflects demand for one platform managing every revenue-related business process efficiently together.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">More News: </span><a href="https://ventureburn.com/convex-raises-57m-series-b/" data-wpel-link="internal"><span style="font-weight: 400">Convex Raises $57M To Build Reliable AI-Native Backend Platform</span></a></p>
<h2><b>Funding Supports Long-Term Product Growth</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Ordway plans enhancing reporting with artificial intelligence forecasting tools covering churn, cash flow, and revenue growth. These tools help finance teams make faster decisions while reducing repetitive manual financial analysis and reporting tasks.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The platform targets artificial intelligence, software-as-a-service, cloud, and subscription businesses managing recurring revenue efficiently worldwide. It also supports organisations using usage-based pricing models alongside traditional recurring subscription billing structures successfully together.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Harbert Growth Partners said artificial intelligence is increasing the complexity of pricing, billing, and monetisation strategies for technology businesses. The investor believes Ordway is well positioned to help finance teams adapt through automation and intelligent financial infrastructure.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Ordway combines payment processing, self-service checkout, subscriber management, investor management, and usage-based billing within one platform. With fresh funding and continued profitability, Ordway aims to strengthen its position as businesses seek more efficient ways to manage increasingly sophisticated revenue operations.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">To stay updated on crypto venture capital funding and market trends, visit our </span><a href="https://ventureburn.com/category/news/venture-capital/" data-wpel-link="internal"><span style="font-weight: 400">venture capital news section</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> for more insights.</span></p>
