		<title>How to Build a Complete Product Marketing Campaign with Pollo AI</title>
		<link>https://ventureburn.com/how-to-build-a-complete-product-marketing-campaign-with-pollo-ai/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Staff Reporter]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Wed, 05 Aug 2026 12:41:57 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[AI]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[News]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://ventureburn.com/?p=204040</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>A product marketing campaign rarely relies on one video alone. A business may need a primary ad to introduce the product, shorter clips for social media, and product visuals for</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/how-to-build-a-complete-product-marketing-campaign-with-pollo-ai/" data-wpel-link="internal">How to Build a Complete Product Marketing Campaign with Pollo AI</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">A product marketing campaign rarely relies on one video alone. A business may need a primary ad to introduce the product, shorter clips for social media, and product visuals for a landing page or online store.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">These assets are often created separately, which can make the process slower and harder to keep consistent. Pollo AI groups its tools into three areas. Marketing Studio is designed for ads and promotional videos, Commerce Studio focuses on product and e-commerce visuals, and Creative Studio provides image and video generation tools for campaigns that begin with an idea rather than finished assets.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The workflow below shows how a team can use these tools to create a connected set of campaign materials without producing more content than the campaign actually needs.</span></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400;">How Can You Create a Main Product Ad in Pollo AI?</span></h2>
<div id="attachment_204044" style="width: 522px" class="wp-caption aligncenter"><img decoding="async" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-204044" class="wp-image-204044 size-full" src="https://ventureburn.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/oavb5820261.jpg" alt="How Can You Create a Main Product Ad in Pollo AI?" width="512" height="290" /><p id="caption-attachment-204044" class="wp-caption-text">Image from Pollo AI</p></div>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The best starting point depends on what the team already has. After opening </span><a href="https://pollo.ai/" data-wpel-link="exclude"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Pollo AI</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;">, go to Marketing Studio and select a workflow based on the available material.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">URL to Video Ads is useful when the product already has a complete online page. Photo to Video Ads is a better fit when there are product images but no video footage. If the campaign copy has already been approved, Script to Ad Video can turn that message into a video.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">These tools serve as different entry points. A campaign normally needs only one of them to create its main ad.</span></p>
<h3><span style="font-weight: 400;">Add the Source Material and Generate the First Version</span></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Paste the product URL, upload the product images, or enter the script, depending on the selected workflow. Then choose the available creative settings and generate the video. If the campaign requires a particular visual approach, users can also explore available models such as the </span><a href="https://pollo.ai/m/goenhance-ai" data-wpel-link="exclude"><span style="font-weight: 400;">GoEnhance AI video generator</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;"> on Pollo AI and select the option that best fits the intended content.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The source material matters. A product page with outdated details or a group of photos showing different product versions can make the result less consistent. It is worth checking these materials before starting rather than correcting the same issue in several generated versions.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">For a short ad, one clear benefit is usually enough. If the product has several important selling points, separate videos can give each one more room instead of forcing everything into a single script.</span></p>
<h3><span style="font-weight: 400;">Create a Second Version with a Different Hook</span></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Once the first ad is ready, generate another version with a different opening.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">For example, one video could begin with a common customer problem, while another could show the product being used immediately. The main message can remain the same.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Keeping most of the content unchanged makes it easier to see whether the opening affects how the video performs.</span></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400;">How Can You Create Supporting Product Assets?</span></h2>
<div id="attachment_204042" style="width: 522px" class="wp-caption aligncenter"><img decoding="async" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-204042" class="wp-image-204042 size-full" src="https://ventureburn.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/oavb5820262.jpg" alt="How Can You Create Supporting Product Assets?" width="512" height="254" /><p id="caption-attachment-204042" class="wp-caption-text">Image from Pollo AI</p></div>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The main ad may attract attention, but customers often need clearer product information before they decide to buy. Product images and showcase videos can fill that gap on product pages, online stores, and social channels.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Open Commerce Studio and select the tool that matches the asset needed. AI Product Shot can create clean product-focused images, while Product Staging can place a product in a lifestyle scene or campaign setting.</span></p>
<h3><span style="font-weight: 400;">Create Product Images and Showcase Videos</span></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Upload the product image, choose or describe the intended presentation, and generate the visual.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">A simple product shot may work better for an online listing, while a lifestyle image can give social content more context. The images do not need to use the same layout, but the product should look consistent throughout the campaign.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">If the product page would benefit from motion, select Product Showcase Video. This can provide a closer look at the product’s design or key features without repeating the main ad.</span></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400;">How Can You Create a Campaign Without Existing Assets?</span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Some campaigns begin before product photos or video footage are available. In this situation, Creative Studio can be used to develop visual concepts from written descriptions.</span></p>
<h3><span style="font-weight: 400;">Develop Concepts with Text to Image or Text to Video</span></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Select Text to Image to explore a campaign’s visual direction. Describe the product, setting, style, and composition, then generate an image that can be used to evaluate the concept.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Select Text to Video when the campaign is built around a scenario or product use case. Describing the main action and environment gives the model a clearer idea of what the scene should show.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">These tools can be useful for testing ideas before arranging a photoshoot or filming. For a real product, however, concept visuals should not be treated as final product images unless the generated details match the item being sold.</span></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400;">How Can You Adapt the Campaign for Different Platforms?</span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">After creating the main ad and supporting visuals, return to Marketing Studio and choose the platform-specific workflow needed for the campaign. Pollo AI includes tools for channels such as TikTok, Instagram, Facebook, and YouTube.</span></p>
<h3><span style="font-weight: 400;">Create Short-Form and UGC-Style Content</span></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">For TikTok or Instagram, use the main campaign message as a starting point, but shorten the setup and bring the product into the video earlier. A quick demonstration, a familiar customer problem, or a strong opening visual can help establish the message.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">If a more personal presentation suits the product, UGC Video Ads can provide another content format. It is not necessary to create content for every platform. The campaign should focus on the channels most relevant to its audience.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The campaign materials do not need to look identical, but they should support the same product message. The main ad can introduce the product, short videos can focus on individual benefits, and product visuals can provide the details customers need on a landing page or online store. Giving each asset a different purpose helps avoid publishing several versions of the same idea.</span></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400;">Conclusion</span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Pollo AI can be used across several parts of a product marketing campaign. Marketing Studio provides starting points for creating ads from product URLs, images, or scripts. Commerce Studio supports product images and showcase videos, while Creative Studio offers Text to Image and Text to Video tools for campaigns that begin with an idea.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">By choosing a workflow based on the materials already available, teams can create a set of related campaign assets without having to build every image and video separately.</span></p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/how-to-build-a-complete-product-marketing-campaign-with-pollo-ai/" data-wpel-link="internal">How to Build a Complete Product Marketing Campaign with Pollo AI</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
			</item>
